/- English proof (translation)
Establish an intermediate fact. Rewrite the hypotheses and the conclusion using the stated equalities. Clear the denominators using the available nonvanishing facts.
-/
theorem term_even (q z : ℂ) (hq : q ≠ 0) (i : ℕ) :
    (z / q ^ 2) ^ (2 * i) * q ^ (2 * i + 2 * (2 * i / 2)) = (z ^ 2) ^ i := by
  have h : 2 * i / 2 = i := by omega
  rw [h, div_pow, ← pow_mul, show 2 * i + 2 * i = 2 * (2 * i) by ring, ← pow_mul]
  field_simp

/- English proof (translation)
Establish an intermediate fact. Rewrite the conclusion using the stated equalities. Establish an intermediate fact. Rewrite the conclusion using the stated equalities. Simplify using the standard rewrite rules.

Rewrite the hypotheses and the conclusion using the stated equalities. Clear the denominators using the available nonvanishing facts. Expand and normalize the polynomial expressions, which then agree.
-/
theorem term_odd (q z : ℂ) (hq : q ≠ 0) (i : ℕ) :
    (z / q ^ 2) ^ (2 * i + 1) * q ^ (2 * i + 1 + 2 * ((2 * i + 1) / 2)) = z / q * (z ^ 2) ^ i := by
  have h : (2 * i + 1) / 2 = i := by omega
  rw [h]
  have h4 : 2 * i + 1 + 2 * i = 2 * (2 * i) + 1 := by ring
  rw [h4]
  simp only [div_pow, ← pow_mul]
  rw [show 2 * (2 * i + 1) = (2 * (2 * i) + 1) + 1 by ring, pow_succ q (2 * (2 * i) + 1)]
  field_simp
  ring

/- English proof (translation)
Establish an intermediate fact. Rewrite the conclusion using the stated equalities. Use the polynomial consequences of the given equalities and inequalities. Establish an intermediate fact. Establish an intermediate fact.

Establish an intermediate fact. Apply function extensionality and compare values at an arbitrary argument. Rewrite the conclusion using the stated equalities. Establish an intermediate fact. Establish an intermediate fact.

